sin heavy chain) identify smooth muscle cells. Together these markers define the mural cell compartment encompassing pericytes and smooth muscle cells.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["STEAP4", "COL25A1", "MYOCD", "MYH11"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["STEAP4", "COL25A1", "MYOCD", "MYH11"], "synonyms": ["unknown"], "categoryFullName": "mural cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0008034", "categoryOntologyTerm": "mural cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}]}, {"name": "lvl3_cell_types", "description": "Level 3 cell type labels (most fine-grained).", "annotationMethod": "manual", "algorithmName": "NA", "algorithmVersion": "NA", "algorithmRepoUrl": "NA", "referenceLocation": "NA", "referenceDescription": "NA", "mode": "cell-labels", "status": "parsed", "labelCount": 6, "order": null, "labels": [{"name": "Capillary ECs", "count": 63014, "color": "#db5f57", "fullName": "capillary endothelial cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0002144", "ontologyTerm": "capillary endothelial cell", "rationale": "PECAM1 (CD31) and CDH5 (VE-cadherin) are pan-endothelial markers essential for cell-cell adhesion and vascular integrity, present across all endothelial subtypes. MECOM and ENPEP further confirm endothelial identity. BTNL9, RBP7, and CA4 are enriched in capillary endothelial cells specifically, with CA4 (carbonic anhydrase 4) being a well-established capillary EC marker in adipose tissue. Together these markers identify capillary ECs and distinguish them from arterial, venous, and lymphatic endothelial subtypes.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["PECAM1", "MECOM", "CDH5", "ENPEP", "BTNL9", "RBP7", "CA4"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["PECAM1", "MECOM", "CDH5", "ENPEP", "BTNL9", "RBP7", "CA4"], "synonyms": ["unknown"], "categoryFullName": "endothelial cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000115", "categoryOntologyTerm": "endothelial cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Lymphatic ECs", "count": 10377, "color": "#d3db57", "fullName": "endothelial cell of lymphatic vessel", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0002138", "ontologyTerm": "endothelial cell of lymphatic vessel", "rationale": "PECAM1 (CD31) and CDH5 (VE-cadherin) are pan-endothelial markers confirming endothelial identity, while MECOM and ENPEP further support this. PROX1 is a transcription factor required for lymphatic endothelial cell specification and maintenance, and LYVE1 (lymphatic vessel endothelial hyaluronan receptor 1) is expressed on the surface of lymphatic endothelial cells and involved in hyaluronan uptake. Together these markers identify lymphatic ECs and distinguish them from capillary, arterial, and venous endothelial subtypes.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["PECAM1", "MECOM", "CDH5", "ENPEP", "PROX1", "LYVE1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["PECAM1", "MECOM", "CDH5", "ENPEP", "PROX1", "LYVE1"], "synonyms": ["LEC", "lymphatic endothelial cell"], "categoryFullName": "endothelial cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000115", "categoryOntologyTerm": "endothelial cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "SMCs", "count": 18867, "color": "#57db5f", "fullName": "smooth muscle cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000192", "ontologyTerm": "smooth muscle cell", "rationale": "MYOCD (myocardin) is a transcription factor driving smooth muscle cell differentiation and is enriched in smooth muscle cells. MYH11 (smooth muscle myosin heavy chain) is a contractile protein with enriched expression in mature smooth muscle cells. Together these markers reliably identify smooth muscle cells within the mural cell compartment and distinguish them from pericytes and other stromal populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["MYOCD", "MYH11"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["MYOCD", "MYH11"], "synonyms": ["SMCs", "non-striated muscle cell", "myocytes smooth muscle", "smooth muscle fiber"], "categoryFullName": "mural cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0008034", "categoryOntologyTerm": "mural cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Pericytes", "count": 24595, "color": "#57d3db", "fullName": "pericyte", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000669", "ontologyTerm": "pericyte", "rationale": "STEAP4 (STEAP family member 4) and COL25A1 (collagen type XXV alpha 1) show enriched expression in pericytes in single-nucleus adipose tissue datasets, and are used here to identify this population. Together these markers identify pericytes within the mural cell compartment and distinguish them from smooth muscle cells and stromal populations in adipose tissue.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["STEAP4", "COL25A1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["STEAP4", "COL25A1"], "synonyms": ["adventitial reticular cell", "pericyte cell", "adventitial cell", "pericyte of Rouget", "cell of Rouget", "ARC"], "categoryFullName": "mural cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0008034", "categoryOntologyTerm": "mural cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Venous ECs", "count": 60837, "color": "#5f57db", "fullName": "vein endothelial cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0002543", "ontologyTerm": "vein endothelial cell", "rationale": "PECAM1 (CD31) and CDH5 (VE-cadherin) are pan-endothelial markers confirming endothelial identity, while MECOM and ENPEP further support this. ACKR1 (atypical chemokine receptor 1, also known as DARC) shows enriched expression in venous endothelial cells and is involved in chemokine scavenging. Together these markers identify venous ECs and distinguish them from capillary, arterial, and lymphatic endothelial subtypes.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["PECAM1", "MECOM", "CDH5", "ENPEP", "ACKR1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["PECAM1", "MECOM", "CDH5", "ENPEP", "ACKR1"], "synonyms": ["venous endothelial cell", "endothelial cell of vein"], "categoryFullName": "endothelial cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000115", "categoryOntologyTerm": "endothelial cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Arterial ECs", "count": 33148, "color": "#db57d3", "fullName": "endothelial cell of artery", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:1000413", "ontologyTerm": "endothelial cell of artery", "rationale": "PECAM1 (CD31) and CDH5 (VE-cadherin) are pan-endothelial markers confirming endothelial identity, while MECOM and ENPEP further support this. PCSK5, GJA5 (connexin 40), and NEBL show enriched expression in arterial endothelial cells, with GJA5 mediating gap junction communication characteristic of arterial vessels. Together these markers identify arterial ECs and distinguish them from capillary, venous, and lymphatic endothelial subtypes.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["PECAM1", "MECOM", "CDH5", "ENPEP", "PCSK5", "GJA5", "NEBL"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["PECAM1", "MECOM", "CDH5", "ENPEP", "PCSK5", "GJA5", "NEBL"], "synonyms": ["arterial endothelial cell"], "categoryFullName": "endothelial cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000115", "categoryOntologyTerm": "endothelial cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}]}]}